          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking"} walking
              morphism
            (
            %a{:href => "#OR24"}> Ozornova &amp; Rovelli 2024
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#CCNW"} Cisinski et al.
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-standing"} free-standing
                morphism
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-living"} free-living
              morphism
            – often denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]
            – is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with two
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            connecting them:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  I =
                  \\left\{
                  0 \to 1
                  \\right\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The walking morphism serves as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial"} combinatorial
            model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space"} directed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %strong directed interval
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong directed interval category
            %strong interval
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong interval category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
                is also used in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+interval"} topological interval
                and in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+theory"} order theory
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/under+categories"} under categories
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+categories"} over categories
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
                in the term
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+groupoid"} interval groupoid
                for the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+isomorphism"} walking isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
                is also used in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+category"} factorization category
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
          %p
            It is also commonly called the
            %strong interval preorder
            or the
            %strong interval poset
            (since it is indeed a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %p
            The walking morphism might also be called the “arrow category” although that term is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} also used
            for a category of functors out of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            The notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            comes from the fact that the walking morphism is also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+number"} ordinal number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %p It also appears as
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the 1-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"}> simplex
                ;
            %li
              %p
                the first
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriental"} oriental
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-globe"} 1-globe
          %p
            Since every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is also an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-category"} (n,r)-category
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,r \geq 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            also as some
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,r)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            and modeled as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_the_boolean_domain Relation to the boolean domain
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝟚
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{2}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
            consisting of two objects
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝟚
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0, 1 \in \mathbb{2}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of the walking morphism, and it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of the walking morphism.
          %h3#directed_univalence Directed univalence
          %p
            Since the groupoid core of the walking morphism is the boolean domain, using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion+principle"} recursion principle
            of the boolean domain, we can recursively define a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:I \to \mathrm{Set}
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_0 = \emptyset
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_1 = \{*\}
            (Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            as it doesn’t preserve
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
          %p
            The walking morphism satisfies
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+univalence"} directed univalence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in I
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi B
                    %mi y
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_y^{B_x}
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{hom}_I(x, y)
          %h3#relation_to_the_walking_commutative_triangle Relation to the walking commutative triangle
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^I
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+commutative+triangle"} walking commutative triangle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[2]
            consisting of three objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0, 1, 2 \in \Delta[2]
            and three morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 01
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_{01}:\mathrm{hom}_{\Delta[2]}(0, 1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 02
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_{02}:\mathrm{hom}_{\Delta[2]}(0, 2)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 12
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_{12}:\mathrm{hom}_{\Delta[2]}(1, 2)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 02
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 12
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 01
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_{02} = h_{12} \circ h_{01}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phoa%27s+principle"} Phoa's principle
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %h3#relation_to_the_walking_isomorphism Relation to the walking isomorphism
          %p
            Inverting the single non-identity arrow of the walking morphism, we obtain the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+isomorphism"} walking isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
          %h2#in_dependent_type_theory  In dependent type theory
          %p
            There are many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            which have a
            %em
              directed interval
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            representing the walking morphism in the sense that given a type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and the fibered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+type"} hom type
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\mathbb{I} \to A\right) \simeq \left(\sum_{x:A} \sum_{y:A} \mathrm{hom}_A(x, y)\right)
          %h3#in_simplicial_type_theory In simplicial type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+type+theory"} simplicial type theory
            %strong directed interval type
            (
            %a{:href => "#RS17"}> Riehl &amp; Shulman 2017
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+total+order"} bounded total order
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            %a{:href => "#GWB24"} Gratzer, Weinberger &amp; Buchholtz 2024
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GWB25"} Gratzer, Weinberger &amp; Buchholtz 2025
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+quasi-coherence"} synthetic quasi-coherence
            for finitely generated
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            is a synthetic category in the sense of being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+type"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rezk+complete+type"} Rezk complete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+type"} Segal type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi 𝕀
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \mathbb{I} \simeq \mathrm{bool}
            which says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of the directed interval is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+booleans"} type of booleans
          %h3#in_binary_parametric_type_theory In binary parametric type theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parametric+type+theory"} parametric type theory
            with binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+parametricity"} internal parametricity
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+parametricity"} modal parametricity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+bridge+types"} binary bridge types
            behave as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+types"} hom types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterogeneous+bridge+types"} heterogeneous bridge types
            behave as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterogeneous+hom+types"} heterogeneous hom types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            are the same as that of the homotopical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+type"} interval type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bridge+types"} bridge types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Br
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Br}_A(x, y)
            instead of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Id}_A(x, y)
            for path constructors and the induction principle.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong directed interval type
              is a type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
              with elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0:\mathbb{I}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1:\mathbb{I}
              and bridge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Br
                      %mi 𝕀
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:\mathrm{Br}_\mathbb{I}(0, 1)
              such that for any type family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P(x))_{x:\mathbb{I}}
              with elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_0:P(0)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1:P(1)
              and heterogeneous bridge
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hBr
                        %mi P
                        %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_h:\mathrm{hBr}_P^h(p_0, p_1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝕀
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\prod_{x:\mathbb{I}} P(x)
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} apd
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hBr
                      %mi P
                      %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(0) \equiv p_0:P(0) \qquad p(1) \equiv p_1:P(1) \qquad \mathrm{apd}_P(p, 0, 1, h) \equiv p_h:\mathrm{hBr}_P^h(p_0, p_1)
            %p
          %p
            In the event that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bridge+types"} bridge types
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+observational+type+theory"} higher observational type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+type"} interval type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \neq 1
            in the directed interval, making the directed interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            different from the homotopical interval type.
          %h2#applications Applications
          %p
            The walking morphism is one of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            category that are not terribly interesting in themselves, but that serve an important role in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            as a whole.
          %p
            For instance a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : F \Rightarrow G
            between two
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F,G : C \to D
            is precisely the same as a strictly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi F
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi η
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C \times \{0\}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{F}}
                  \\\
                  C \times I &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\to}&amp; D
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{G}}
                  \\\
                  C \times \{1\}
                  }
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            Accordingly, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi iso
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{iso}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+isomorphism"} walking isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : F \Rightarrow G
            is the same as a diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi F
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi iso
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi η
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C \times \{0\}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{F}}
                  \\\
                  C \times I_{iso} &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\to}&amp; D
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{G}}
                  \\\
                  C \times \{1\}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            Dually, forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Arr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Arr(D) := [I,D]
          %p
            from the walking morphism produces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is also the same as a diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi F
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi η
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi I
                          %mo ,
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi G
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; D \times \{0\}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{F}}\nearrow &amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  C &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\to}&amp; [I,D]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{G}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; D \times \{1\}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            replaced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi iso
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{iso}
            this is again a natural isomorphism, now represented as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+homotopy"} right homotopy
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %p
            The analogous statements are true in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %div
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+structure"} walking structure
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+domain"} boolean domain
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mo ≔
                              %mo ∂
                              %msup
                                %mi Δ
                                %mn 1
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \coloneqq \partial \Delta^1
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                      of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+interval+category"} directed interval category
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi I
                              %mo ≔
                              %msup
                                %mi Δ
                                %mn 1
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \coloneqq \Delta^1
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  %li
                    %p
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C0%29-horn+category"} (2,0)-horn category
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi Λ
                                %mn 0
                                %mn 2
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_0^2
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
